      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.8,
      "end_seconds": 4.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Good morning. I hope the wait wasn't too long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 5.94,
      "end_seconds": 10.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "doctor, um, thank you for seeing us"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.77,
      "end_seconds": 18.78,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. What was the main thing you wanted to talk about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 20.5,
      "end_seconds": 25.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "We came because of pain in my right ankle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.14,
      "end_seconds": 28.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "how far back does it go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.7,
      "end_seconds": 33.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I've had it for three days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.61,
      "end_seconds": 42.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.6,
      "end_seconds": 68.08,
      "duration_seconds": 24.48,
      "text": "a six out of ten, I suppose. Putting weight on it and walking definitely sets it off i didn't want to make a fuss, you know oh, you know, and difficulty walking that's been about the same, five days with difficulty walking, I'd call it moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.96,
      "end_seconds": 70.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Have you had bruising?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.11,
      "end_seconds": 80.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "yes, actually. There was a twist during football, yes, but that went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.66,
      "end_seconds": 96.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Have you had any pain at the back of the heel or pop or crack?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.88,
      "end_seconds": 101.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "right, no, not any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.56,
      "end_seconds": 107.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "right have you had any numbness pain in the knee or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.85,
      "end_seconds": 113.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "no, no numbness, pain in the knee or fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.81,
      "end_seconds": 118.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.0,
      "end_seconds": 121.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "no weakness or anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.68,
      "end_seconds": 125.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.76,
      "end_seconds": 128.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "no problems with breathing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.03,
      "end_seconds": 134.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "are there any allergies on your record that I should check?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.4,
      "end_seconds": 146.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "I I think I reacted to some antibiotic once years ago i don't remember which one or what happened exactly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.79,
      "end_seconds": 152.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "alright do your parents or siblings have any long-term illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.01,
      "end_seconds": 155.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "My mother has migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.91,
      "end_seconds": 159.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "have you got any chronic problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.24,
      "end_seconds": 174.48,
      "duration_seconds": 13.24,
      "text": "Yes an enlarged prostate. I kept putting it off which I know isn't sensible. I mean um I've got heart failure. Sorry I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.43,
      "end_seconds": 185.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "Right, right. Alright, an enlarged prostate and heart failure, that matches what I have here. Have you had to have anything operated on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.57,
      "end_seconds": 192.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "I had cataract surgery on my right eye last year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.55,
      "end_seconds": 197.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Tell me what you take day to day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.76,
      "end_seconds": 209.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate. I'm on spironolactone, 25 milligrams, maybe, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.56,
      "end_seconds": 216.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.08,
      "end_seconds": 225.78,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Paracetamol. I take it it 500 milligrams when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.85,
      "end_seconds": 240.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "right, how about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.24,
      "end_seconds": 244.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.45,
      "end_seconds": 248.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "alright do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.17,
      "end_seconds": 254.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.76,
      "end_seconds": 257.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "do you have a job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.32,
      "end_seconds": 261.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "I'm a self-employed electrician"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.89,
      "end_seconds": 264.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "right, who do you live with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.64,
      "end_seconds": 271.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "I live with my family, my husband and two kids"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.91,
      "end_seconds": 278.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "How do you eat generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.84,
      "end_seconds": 282.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "I skip breakfast most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.15,
      "end_seconds": 285.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.23,
      "end_seconds": 297.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "okay, give me a moment.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.07,
      "end_seconds": 321.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.31,
      "text": "okay: blood pressure 124 over 79 pulse is 74 beats a minute respiratory rate 15 temperature is 36.4 degrees SpO2 97 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.04,
      "end_seconds": 325.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.53,
      "end_seconds": 327.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.71,
      "end_seconds": 330.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Hold that position for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.67,
      "end_seconds": 349.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "There's swelling and bruising on the outer side of the ankle tender over the ligament."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.35,
      "end_seconds": 351.05,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.05,
      "end_seconds": 355.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "tell me if anything hurts"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.94,
      "end_seconds": 371.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "The bones themselves aren't tender and the ankle feels stable when I test it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.31,
      "end_seconds": 377.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "that's all I need thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.01,
      "end_seconds": 406.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "from what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with an ankle sprain at this stage a ligament tear is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.4,
      "end_seconds": 411.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Hmm, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.57,
      "end_seconds": 443.76,
      "duration_seconds": 30.19,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now an ankle sprain is my leading thought, not anything worse let's book an X-ray of the ankle to look into ankle injury what I'm giving you is ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, three times a day after food, for three days that's for ankle pain i'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.65,
      "end_seconds": 467.31,
      "duration_seconds": 22.66,
      "text": "rest, ice for twenty minutes at a time, a compression bandage and keep the foot up. I'll also refer you to physiotherapy. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's review you in two weeks. Alright, I'll see you out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 468.44,
      "end_seconds": 471.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "nothing more from me, thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 472.81,
      "end_seconds": 474.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}